<body>
    <h1>Release Process</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>AI+ RELEASE PROCESS =E2=80=94 RCs, PROMOTION, AND PATCHES</p>
<p>(Updated for single =E2=80=9Crelease/X.Y.Z=E2=80=9D branch per version +=
 optional base_ref)</p>
<p>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>OVERVIEW &amp; CONVENTIONS</p></li>
</ol>
<hr>
<ul>
<li>
<p>One branch per version line:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; release/X.Y.Z</p></li>
</ul>
<p>(Example: release/1.2.0, release/1.2.1, etc.)</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>RCs and final builds are tags:&nbsp; &nbsp; vX.Y.Z-rc1, vX.Y.Z-rc2, =E2=
=80=A6, vX.Y.Z</p></li>
</ul>
<p>(Example: v1.2.0-rc1, v1.2.0-rc2, v1.2.0)</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Normalization: RCs DO NOT create separate branches.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>All RCs for 1.2.0 live on the same branch: release/1.2.0</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>base_ref (optional):</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A tag/branch/commit to start from (e.g., v1.1.1 or release/1.2.0).</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>If omitted, new lines default to main/master.</p></li>
<li>
<p>For patch lines, ALWAYS start from the last final tag (e.g., v1.2.0).</p=
></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Final tags are immutable. If a problem is found after promotion, bump th=
e</p></li>
</ul>
<p>PATCH version and start a new RC (e.g., 1.2.1-rc1 from v1.2.0).</p>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-2)PREREQUISITES"><strong>2) PREREQUISITES</strong>=
</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>GitHub CLI installed and authenticated (gh auth login).</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Org-level workflows live in the .github repo; build_releases.sh calls:</=
p></li>
</ul>
<p>gh workflow run create_release.yml =E2=80=93repo workflow-intelligence-n=
exus/.github</p>
<p>=E2=80=93ref cicd-integration</p>
<p>(Change =E2=80=93ref if the workflow is on another branch.)</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Required token/permissions are already wired as RELEASE_WORKFLOW_GITHUB_=
TOKEN.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D.1"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-3)BUILDANEWMINORRELEASECANDIDATE(e.g.,1.2.0-rc1)">=
<strong>3) BUILD A NEW MINOR RELEASE CANDIDATE (e.g., 1.2.0-rc1)</strong></=
h2>
<p>Default (cut from main/master):</p>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.2.0-rc1</p>
<p></p>
<p>Freeze at a specific point (tag/branch/commit):</p>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.2.0-rc1 &lt;base_ref&gt;</p>
<p></p>
<p>Result:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Creates/updates release/1.2.0</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Creates tag v1.2.0-rc1</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p>During stabilization:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Land fixes on release/1.2.0 (via PRs or cherry-picks).</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Re-spin RC as needed:</p></li>
</ul>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.2.0-rc2</p>
<p>(Do not pass base_ref for re-spins; the workflow will reuse release/1.2.=
0.)</p>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D.2"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-4)PROMOTEARELEASECANDIDATETOFINAL"><strong>4) PROM=
OTE A RELEASE CANDIDATE TO FINAL</strong></h2>
<p>When the chosen RC (e.g., rc2) is approved:</p>
<p>./scripts/promote_release.sh 1.2.0-rc2</p>
<p></p>
<p>Result:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Creates final tag v1.2.0 (immutable)</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D.3"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-5)PATCHAPROMOTEDRELEASE(e.g.,produce1.2.1-rc1fromv=
1.2.0)"><strong>5) PATCH A PROMOTED RELEASE (e.g., produce 1.2.1-rc1 from v=
1.2.0)</strong></h2>
<p></p>
<p>Start from the last final tag (NOT from main):</p>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.2.1-rc1 v1.2.0</p>
<p></p>
<p>Result:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Creates/updates release/1.2.1</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Creates tag v1.2.1-rc1</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<p>Bring in only the required fixes (example cherry-pick flow):</p>
<p>git fetch =E2=80=93all =E2=80=93tags</p>
<p>git checkout release/1.2.1</p>
<p>git cherry-pick -x&nbsp; [=E2=80=A6]</p>
<p>git push</p>
<p></p>
<p>If you added commits after v1.2.1-rc1 already exists, either:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Move the RC tag (allowed for RCs you control):</p></li>
</ul>
<p>git tag -d v1.2.1-rc1 &amp;&amp; git push origin :refs/tags/v1.2.1-rc1</=
p>
<p>git tag -a v1.2.1-rc1 -m =E2=80=9CUpdate RC after hotfixes=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>git push origin v1.2.1-rc1</p>
<p>OR</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Create the next RC:</p></li>
</ul>
<p>git tag -a v1.2.1-rc2 -m =E2=80=9CSecond RC=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>git push origin v1.2.1-rc2</p>
<p></p>
<p>Promote when ready:</p>
<p>./scripts/promote_release.sh 1.2.1-rcX</p>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D.4"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-6)QUICKDECISIONMATRIX"><strong>6) QUICK DECISION M=
ATRIX</strong></h2>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Start new minor line (e.g., 1.3.0-rc1):</p></li>
</ul>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.3.0-rc1</p>
<p>(No base_ref =E2=86=92 cut from main/master, or pass a freeze ref.)</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Re-spin RC on same minor (e.g., 1.3.0-rc2):</p></li>
</ul>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.3.0-rc2</p>
<p>(Reuses release/1.3.0.)</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Promote RC to final:</p></li>
</ul>
<p>./scripts/promote_release.sh 1.3.0-rcN</p>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Patch a promoted minor (e.g., 1.3.1-rc1):</p></li>
</ul>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.3.1-rc1 v1.3.0</p>
<p>(ALWAYS base from the last final tag.)</p>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D.5"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-7)BESTPRACTICES&amp;NOTES"><strong>7) BEST PRACTIC=
ES &amp; NOTES</strong></h2>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Don=E2=80=99t merge main wholesale into a patch line; cherry-pick only w=
hat you need.</p></li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Projects that embed a version (package.json, pyproject.toml, etc.) must =
be</p></li>
</ul>
<p>bumped on the release/X.Y.Z branch before publishing artifacts.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Old RC-suffixed branches from before this policy (e.g., release/1.1.1-rc=
1)</p></li>
</ul>
<p>can be cleaned up once unused:</p>
<p>git push origin :release/1.1.1-rc1</p>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D.6"><strong>=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D</strong></h2>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-8)FAQ"><strong>8) FAQ</strong></h2>
<p>Q: What exactly is base_ref?</p>
<p>A: Any tag/branch/commit in the TARGET repo used as the starting point f=
or the</p>
<p>release branch. Examples: v1.1.1, release/1.2.0, a specific SHA. If omit=
ted,</p>
<p>new minor lines are cut from main/master.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Q: For RC re-spins, do I need base_ref?</p>
<p>A: No. The workflow will switch to the existing release/X.Y.Z branch if =
it</p>
<p>exists and use that head. (It briefly checks out main/master first, then=
</p>
<p>checks out and fast-forwards release/X.Y.Z.)</p>
<p></p>
<p>Q: Can I promote more than once?</p>
<p>A: No. Final tags (e.g., v1.2.0) are immutable. If an issue is found aft=
er</p>
<p>promotion, bump PATCH and start a new RC (e.g., 1.2.1-rc1 from v1.2.0).<=
/p>
<p></p>
<p>Q: Is it okay to move RC tags?</p>
<p>A: Yes, if your team controls the consumers. Delete and recreate the RC =
tag at</p>
<p>the desired commit. Do NOT move final tags.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Q: Which branch of the .github repo runs the workflow?</p>
<p>A: build_releases.sh uses =E2=80=93ref cicd-integration by default. Chan=
ge it if your</p>
<p>workflow is on another branch.</p>
<p></p>
<p>Q: How do I verify what I=E2=80=99m building from?</p>
<p>A:</p>
<p>git tag -l v1.2.0</p>
<p>git show =E2=80=93no-patch =E2=80=93decorate v1.2.0</p>
<p>git branch -r =E2=80=93contains v1.2.0</p>
<p>git log =E2=80=93oneline v1.2.0..origin/main &nbsp; # what changed on ma=
in since final</p>
<p></p>
<p>Q: What if I need to freeze 1.2.0 earlier than current main?</p>
<p>A: Pass a base_ref (tag/branch/commit) when creating 1.2.0-rc1:</p>
<p>./scripts/build_releases.sh 1.2.0-rc1 &lt;base_ref&gt;</p>
<h2 id=3D"ReleaseProcess-=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
